# examples = list of kwargs dicts; expected values are produced by refs.S (reference solutions) in gen.py and executed again by check_examples.py.
GG="Graph pattern guides and lists (techinterview.org graph interview patterns and comprehensive graph guides, DesignGurus common graph-traversal questions, Techie Delight graph practice list; search snippets only, not opened)"
CK="Candidate-reported rounds on Naukri Code360 and GeeksforGeeks (a Flipkart 2021 report with number of islands, a Flipkart 2025 online assessment and a GeeksforGeeks on-campus 2020 report with word ladder; search-result summaries only, pages not opened; self-reported, unverified)"
PQ="Dijkstra and lazy-deletion write-ups (a PracHub guide on Dijkstra stale heap entries and negative edges, Codeforces lazy-deletion tutorials, a python-dev heapq thread; search snippets only, not opened; docs.python.org was unreachable)"
ED="Standard-problem lists known to the editor (not found as an opened page; indicative only, no company attribution)"
REC="Sizes are chosen so that a recursive DFS would exceed CPython's default recursion limit of 1000, so an iterative method (queue or explicit stack) is required."
