q(3,'🟡','dsu_ops',"Union-find with path compression and union by size. Nodes are 0..n-1 (1 <= n <= 10^5) and `ops` is a list of up to 2*10^5 operations, each [kind, a, b] with kind 'union' or 'connected'. For 'union', merge the sets of a and b and report True if they were different sets (a merge happened) or False if already together; for 'connected', report whether a and b are in the same set without changing anything. Return `[results, num_sets, largest_set]`: the list of reported booleans in operation order, the number of sets at the end and the size of the largest set at the end. `find` must be iterative (a chain of unions without union by size can build a path of 10^5 nodes, beyond the recursion limit of 1000). State the amortised cost (inverse Ackermann) and why compression alone, or by-size alone, is already good.",
 [{'n':5,'ops':[['union',0,1],['union',1,2],['connected',0,2],['union',0,2],['connected',3,4]]},{'n':1,'ops':[['union',0,0],['connected',0,0]]},{'n':3,'ops':[]}],GG+' | '+ED)
